  "description": "The name of a space, a collection or a group is a kem1 envelope under the space key's child: name_key = HKDF-SHA256(space_key, salt = absent, info = \"kemlock/v1/space-name\", L = 32); ciphertext = nonce(12) || AES-256-GCM(name_key, nonce, text as UTF-8, aad) with the 16-byte tag at the end; aad = \"kemlock/v1/item\" || id || u64be(key_version) || lp(kind) || owner, where id is the object's own id (space_id for the space's name), kind is \"space-name\", \"collection-name\" or \"group-name\", owner is 0x02 || space_id and key_version is the space key version. There is no item-key wrap: name_key is the item key. A name must not open under another space, id, kind, key version or owner.",
